==============================================================================
S665 address-coordinate derivative repair atlas
==============================================================================

Grammar
  1. find a scalar/product collision
  2. attach the missing fraction/address coordinate
  3. unroll it back into a derivative sum

A. Source anchors
  explicit formulae for L-functions: Euler product/log-derivative prime-power sums plus zero sums
    https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Explicit_formulae_for_L-functions
  graph reconstruction algebraic formulation: deck collisions, Kocay linear constraints, covering-number matrices
    https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.4121
  graph reconstruction pair parameters: new reconstructible vertex-pair address parameters
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.00620
  inverse spectral Weyl m-function: m-function/spectral measure determines potential and has A-equation
    https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9906118
  structured matrices and continued fractions: Hankel matrices, moment problems, J-fractions, root localization
    https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/090781127
  continued fractions and Hankel determinants: continued fractions generate Hankel determinant formulae and Lax pairs
    https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.05204
  Tutte polynomial deletion-contraction: deletion-contraction and activity-address expansions
    https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/reference/algorithms/generated/networkx.algorithms.polynomials.tutte_polynomial.html
  Hodge theory for combinatorial geometries: matroid Chow-ring address proves log-concavity of characteristic coefficients
    https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.02888
  Selberg trace formula: spectrum/geodesic trace formula as closed-orbit derivative sum
    https://mathworld.wolfram.com/SelbergTraceFormula.html

