D. Exact-ish lanes
  LRC14 Res27 carry
    collision:  same Res27 additive/product shadow mixes floor and strict rows
    address:    carry word k in v=r+27k plus owner/continuant state
    derivative: carry-deletion derivative deck: M, wall pairs, gcd mass, apex and owner losses
    next:       attach HYP-2165 owner routes and test deeper carry perturbations
  Tournament deck paired owner
    collision:  full decks and global scalar repairs collide through n=6
    address:    paired card address (card isomorphism type, deleted vertex outdegree)
    derivative: deleted-score, H-loss, and c3-loss sums paired to each card
    next:       extend paired derivative minimality to n=7 with canonical augmentation
  Graph reconstruction Kocay matrix
    collision:  many graphs may share coarse deck-derived product/scalar shadows
    address:    covering-number or vertex-pair parameter address rows
    derivative: Kocay-style linear constraints and recursive pair-parameter equations
    next:       port paired derivative deck tests from tournaments to ordinary graphs
  Riemann/Weil explicit formula
    collision:  Euler product alone hides zero/gamma/infinity address data
    address:    zeros, gamma factor, and test-function/Fourier address
    derivative: logarithmic derivative turns products into prime-power and zero sums
    next:       use as the model for product-ledger -> derivative-sum transformations
  Ihara/Selberg graph zeta
    collision:  determinant/product zeta can collide at spectral level
    address:    primitive closed geodesic or scattering/geodesic-length address
    derivative: log derivative/trace formula expands product into closed-orbit sums
    next:       compute Ihara/Bartholdi zeta for small tournament-derived graphs
  Stieltjes moment J-fraction
    collision:  moment/Hankel scalar data can be indeterminate or too coarse
    address:    continued-fraction coefficients and Hankel determinant address
    derivative: J-fraction/orthogonal-polynomial recurrence unrolls into moment sums
    next:       build a finite moment-collision toy beside OCF independence packets
  Inverse spectral Weyl m-function
    collision:  spectrum/product data alone needs norming or spectral measure address
    address:    Weyl m-function or spectral measure
    derivative: m-function expansion and A-equation unroll potential into derivative/integral sums
    next:       use m-function as archetype for LRC owner address, not just analogy
  Pi/e Vieta branch sheet
    collision:  trace/norm pair leaves root order or branch sheet unresolved
    address:    discriminant D=e-pi or finite-field branch x-y
    derivative: Newton power sums and branch derivative split the two sheets
    next:       reuse finite-field branch lab as a generic collision detector
  OCF noncommutative address
    collision:  commutative OCF H=I(Omega,2) forgets vertex/set-partition addresses
    address:    noncommuting variables and set partitions
    derivative: deletion-contraction in the richer W_X unrolls to OCF packet sums
    next:       test transfer-matrix symmetry by projecting NC identities downward
  Finite-field Kakeya pinned owner
    collision:  full distance support saturates while union size and pinned minima vary
    address:    pin owner, line-choice recursion, concurrency label
    derivative: pinned-distance and concurrency derivative sums
    next:       classify full-distance-support twins by owner labels
  Union-closed frequency pressure
    collision:  frequency vectors collide at m=4
    address:    set pressure address sum_B |A union B|
    derivative: pressure-loss derivative over added/deleted sets
    next:       classify frequency collision buckets by pressure derivative profile
  Goldbach/Lemoine pair plane
    collision:  even E=p+q and odd O=p+2q are separate scalar columns
    address:    ordered pair address q=O-E, p=2E-O
    derivative: parent-rich odd/even companion sums and swap-reflection derivative
    next:       rank shared prime-pair columns by local sieve plus reconstruction address
  A000568 marked observer fiber
    collision:  unmarked tournament classes and scalar counts mix LRC status
    address:    rooted/marked observer fiber and endpoint threshold labels
    derivative: source/deletion/gap-threshold derivative sums
    next:       use address-coordinate grammar for every quotient count

